# CVEN Equity Value & Share Price Model

To move from **Enterprise Value (EV)** to **Equity Value** and ultimately a **share price**, use the standard valuation framework:

```text
Enterprise Value
+ Cash
- Debt
= Equity Value
```

---

# Capital Structure Assumptions

### Year 10

| Item | $ Billions |
|--------|--------:|
| Enterprise Value | 24.0 |
| Cash Balance | 11.1 |
| Debt | 1.0 |
| Equity Value | 34.1 |

Formula:

```text
24.0
+11.1
-1.0
=
34.1 Billion
```

---

# Fully Diluted Share Count

Assume the company is structured as follows:

| Security Type | Shares (Millions) |
|--------------|------------------:|
| Founders | 600 |
| Employees/ESOP | 150 |
| Seed Investors | 75 |
| Series A | 75 |
| Series B | 60 |
| Series C | 40 |

Total Fully Diluted Shares:

```text
1,000 Million Shares
```

or

```text
1.0 Billion Shares
```

---

# Base Case Share Price

```text
Equity Value
÷
Diluted Shares
=
Share Price
```

Calculation:

```text
$34.1 Billion
÷
1.0 Billion
=
$34.10/share
```

